Almost certainly a troll posting. Nethack requires disk I/O. Along with
the library to do ansii graphics. That requires an operating system.
There *is* however an add-on for fsck (pretty much defunct since linux
kernel 2.6) that allows you to play tetris while it's checking your
partition for errors however. If you're not familiar with linux, before
kernel 2.6 linux would run what could best be described as a *very* full
scandisk on your linux partition. Every 5-10 boots roughly. That's what
fsck would do. I can't recall the exact number (which you could change). 

It *is* theoretically possible to have nethack running without an OS, but
that would require re-writing it. In assembly language.

